course: dictionary
lesson: 9496
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stem is the long thin part of a plant that holds up the leaves and flowers. «The crushed cane stems left over are burned to power the sugar mills.» Here the stems are the plant parts left after the juice is pressed out, so context tells you which meaning is meant.
explain: One word can have several meanings. A stem can also be the thin part of a wine glass or an apple stalk. In grammar, the stem is the main part of a word before endings are added: play is the stem of playing.
explain: Stem can be a verb too. To stem from means to come from or be caused by. Test each meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it does not make sense, try the next meaning.
fact: A stem is the long thin part of a plant that holds up the leaves and flowers.
fact: Stems carry water and food between the roots and the leaves. Put a white carnation in blue ink and its petals turn blue, because the stem carried the coloured water up.
fact: In grammar, the stem is the main part of a word before endings are added.
fact: To stem from means to come from or be caused by.
fact: STEM means science, technology, engineering and maths.
exercise: «The crushed cane stems left over are burned to power the sugar mills.» In this sentence, what are the stems? | The handles of kitchen spoons | The thin stems of wine glasses | The leaves of a tree | *The plant parts left over after the juice is pressed out
exercise: In the word «playing», what is the stem? | *play | gaming | playing | ing
exercise: «The cold might stem from the damp weather.» What does stem from mean? | To count in tens | To grow a long thin part | To stop growing | *To come from or be caused by
test: «A stem-and-leaf plot shows numbers split into tens and ones.» In this plot, what does the stem show? | The total of all the numbers | The decimal point | The ones | *The tens
test: What does STEM stand for? | Stems, trees, earth and mud | Sport, travel, eating and mapping | Stories, text, English and music | *Science, technology, engineering and maths
exam: «A potato is a swollen stem, not a root.» In this sentence, what is a potato? | A leaf | A flower | A root | *A swollen stem
